<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hwangsanbeol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/660">660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hwangsanbeol was fought in 660 near present-day Nonsan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> between a large Silla army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-yu-sin">Kim Yu-sin</a> and a small Baekje force led by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyebaek">Gyebaek</a>. After several Baekje successes, Gyebaek was killed and his army destroyed. With a Tang army landing at the same time, the Baekje capital Sabi fell within days, ending the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hwangsanbeol.jpg" alt="Battle of Hwangsanbeol" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Three_Kingdoms_of_Korea_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
